n", -0.002241977024823427], [" session", -7.666252136230469]]}], "text": "Here's a summary of the session notes in 8 bullet points:\n\n- **Scope & context:** A two-part rebuild series of the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D + Intel Arc A770 16GB), spanning 2026-09-26 to 2026-10-01 across two Claude contexts (Opus 5.5 then Sonnet 5.5), covering oneAPI 2026.0\u21922026.1, oneDNN A/B, SYCL graphs, and kernel tuning.\n\n- **Major technical challenges addressed:** The session tackled an LLAMA_SUBPROCESS ABI trap (d37dd50bb), SYCL graphs, an IGC crash requiring a DG2 XMX-gather patch (4e7400c3a), 256-GRF kernels, and a \"12-vs-18 t/s decode investigation,\" plus a DLE swap during the oneAPI 2026.1 upgrade.\n\n- **Driver transition:** The Arc A770 switched from i915 to the **xe** driver between the two contexts (handled by other sessions), with the host running kernel 7.3.0-rc5 with xe binding [verified live].\n\n- **Extensive benchmarking:** Multiple benchmark rounds were run (including llama-bench and perplexity A/B tests), with data stored in `~/research-llama.cpp/sycl-oneapi-benchmarks-2026-09-27/` and `\u2026-2026-10-01/`.\n\n- **Comprehensive documentation"}